# LifePunch Rules Workflow

- Rule content and worker deploy edits happen in **Rules-V1.txt** (production).
- Canonical paths:
  - Repo: `lifepunch/website/deployments/Rules/Rules-V1.txt`
  - OneDrive deploy paste: `OneDrive/Documents/Lifepunch/Rules/Rules-V1.txt`
- Keep the repo and OneDrive copies of Rules-V1.txt in sync when changing rules.
- **`cloudflare-worker.mjs`** should stay aligned with Rules-V1.txt for rules and rules UI; merge in worker-only code (auth, store, webhooks) — do not blind-overwrite.
- Regenerate **`current-rules.md`** from V1 with `lifepunch/website/deployments/scripts/build-current-rules-md.mjs` when rule content changes.
- **Rules-Test1.txt** is an optional sandbox — copy V1 → Test1 before risky experiments; copy Test1 → V1 only when promoting validated changes.
- **Rules-V2.txt** is a layout comparison prototype only — numbered rules (V1) vs bullet/no-numeral layout. Use it to show someone both options and pick a direction. Do not hand-edit V2. Regenerate from V1 with `lifepunch/website/deployments/scripts/build-rules-v2-copy.mjs` only when actively refreshing that side-by-side comparison.
- V2 is not part of the normal promote/deploy path unless you decide to adopt that layout as production.
- `LP_RULES` lives inside the worker source in Rules-V1.txt. Prefer editing V1 over duplicate one-off worker copies.
- Cloudflare paste deploy uses Rules-V1.txt (full worker, not partial).
